From 2bf8579d2139679f80f5aad6a0d910800c910a1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Certe Kim <18364439+CerteKim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:50:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: do not gate the GMU clocks from the GPU PM
 paths

15cc59ac954e ("drm/msm/a6xx: Add support for Adreno 612") added

	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(gmu->nr_clocks, gmu->clocks);

to a6xx_pm_suspend() and the matching clk_bulk_prepare_enable() to
a6xx_pm_resume().

The GMU is its own runtime-PM device (2c6a000.gmu plus its genpd
wrappers): its clocks are prepared/enabled by a6xx_gmu_resume() and
released by a6xx_gmu_stop() -> a6xx_hfi_stop().  Disabling them a second
time from the *GPU's* suspend path drops the GMU's clock while the GMU
device is still runtime-active, so the CM3 core stops executing while its
register block (GDSC powered) stays readable.

That is exactly the state seen on the Xiaomi Book S 12.4 (SC8180X, a680)
a few seconds after GNOME starts rendering: the HFI command queue still
holds an unconsumed GX_BW_PERF_VOTE (read_index frozen), the response
queue is empty, yet the GPU and GMU registers read back fine - the GMU
simply never looks at the queue again and the watchdog fires ~5s later.
6.18, which does not touch the GMU clocks here, runs GNOME on the same
board without any of this.

The GMU's clocks are owned by the GMU device, so leave them to it.
Revert this hunk if Adreno 612 turns out to need the programming - that
board is not this one.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
index b723c87d8481..1515c7c92d5f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
@@ -2191,12 +2191,6 @@ static int a6xx_pm_resume(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_put_gxpd;
 
-	ret = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(gmu->nr_clocks, gmu->clocks);
-	if (ret) {
-		clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(gpu->nr_clocks, gpu->grp_clks);
-		goto err_put_gxpd;
-	}
-
 	if (adreno_is_a619_holi(adreno_gpu))
 		a6xx_sptprac_enable(gmu);
 
@@ -2269,7 +2263,6 @@ static int a6xx_pm_suspend(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 		a6xx_sptprac_disable(gmu);
 
 	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(gpu->nr_clocks, gpu->grp_clks);
-	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(gmu->nr_clocks, gmu->clocks);
 
 	pm_runtime_put_sync(gmu->gxpd);
 	dev_pm_opp_set_opp(&gpu->pdev->dev, NULL);
